@startuml anchor-exclusive-flag-lifecycle
' ============================================================================
' The provenance flag of one AnchorRoot after bug 14492 (stack-safety report
' section 5.60.7, "Flag lifecycle").
'   GREEN  #2E7D32  exclusive: one wrapper and the flag set; the gate answers Removed
'   AMBER  #EF6C00  the flag set but a second wrapper alive; the gate answers Shared
'   RED    #C62828  the flag cleared by a header clone; the gate answers Shared
'   BLUE   #1565C0  creation of an anchor: construction, rebuild or header clone
'   GREY   #616161  the final drop and its guarded drain
' w(a) is the anchor's wrapper count and f(a) its flag. R5 and R6 are bug
' 14492's rulings: wrapper clones leave the flag alone, and
' normalize_live_empty never sets it again.
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontSize 12
}

title <b>Provenance flag of one anchor</b>\nset when the anchor is built, cleared on both anchors by a header clone, never set again

state "Exclusive" as Exclusive #C8E6C9
Exclusive : <latex>w(a) = 1,\ f(a) = \mathrm{true}</latex>
Exclusive : the gate answers ""Removed""
state "Aliased" as Aliased #FFE0B2
Aliased : <latex>w(a) \ge 2,\ f(a) = \mathrm{true}</latex>
Aliased : the gate answers ""Shared"": ""Arc::get_mut"" fails,
Aliased : so an exhausting removal falls back, and its
Aliased : wrapper moves to a fresh exclusive anchor.
Aliased : Wrapper clones, and drops or fallbacks that
Aliased : leave <latex>w(a) \ge 2</latex>, keep the anchor here.
state "Cleared" as Cleared #FFCDD2
Cleared : <latex>f(a) = \mathrm{false}</latex>, any <latex>w(a) \ge 1</latex>
Cleared : the gate answers ""Shared"" for the rest of the
Cleared : anchor's life, so every exhausting removal falls
Cleared : back, and its wrapper moves to a fresh exclusive anchor.
Cleared : Wrapper clones, drops and writes keep the anchor here.

[*] -[#1565C0,thickness=2]-> Exclusive : ""new_with_barrier"" calls ""from_map"",\nwhich builds around ""PathMap::new()"";\na fallback rebuild ends the same way
[*] -[#1565C0,thickness=2]-> Cleared : a header clone creates the copy,\nwhich starts cleared
Exclusive -[#2E7D32]-> Exclusive : in-place removal; a write, whose\n""make_mut"" clones nothing;\n""normalize_live_empty"" leaves the flag (R6)
Exclusive -[#EF6C00]-> Aliased : wrapper clone (""Arc::clone""),\nflag unchanged (R5)
Aliased -[#2E7D32]-> Exclusive : a drop or a fallback leaves one\nwrapper: <latex>w(a) = 1</latex> again
Aliased -[#C62828,thickness=2]-> Cleared : a write through one wrapper takes a header clone:\n""AnchorRoot::clone"" stores false first (Release),\nand the writer moves to the cleared copy
Exclusive -[#616161]-> [*] : last wrapper dropped:\nthe guarded drain
Cleared -[#616161]-> [*] : last wrapper dropped:\nthe guarded drain

note right of Aliased #FFF3E0
  A short-lived read-only clone does not
  disable the in-place path after it drops:
  the ""Arc::get_mut"" conjunct refuses
  only while the clone lives.
end note

note left of Cleared #FFEBEE
  The anchor cannot tell whether the other
  version still shares its nodes, so the flag
  stays cleared; the next fallback rebuild
  gives the Bag a fresh exclusive anchor.
  Cost: at most one <latex>\Theta(B + M)</latex> rebuild
  per Bag per soft checkpoint.
end note
@enduml
